From: devcore94 <ditternation@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] camera: avoid Clang 22 CSI v4 optimizer crash

The AOSP Clang 22 toolchain can crash in the simplifycfg optimizer while
compiling is-device-csi_v4.c, specifically the is_isr_csi() function. Keep
the workaround local to this object so the rest of the kernel retains its
normal optimization level.

Signed-off-by: devcore94 <ditternation@outlook.com>

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/exynos/camera/Makefile b/drivers/media/platform/exynos/camera/Makefile
--- a/drivers/media/platform/exynos/camera/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/exynos/camera/Makefile
@@ -58,6 +58,8 @@ ifeq ($(CONFIG_EXYNOS_DEVICE_MIPI_CSIS_VER4),y)
 fimc-is-objs += is-device-csi_v4.o
 endif
 
+CFLAGS_is-device-csi_v4.o += -O1
+
 ifeq ($(CONFIG_VIDEO_EXYNOS_PABLO_ISP),m)
 fimc-is-objs += is-mem_v2.o
 else
